WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:05.307
Daisy and Kaleem discussed the case as they headed home.

2
00:00:05.308 --> 00:00:09.776
"We already talked to all the animals in the neighborhood," Daisy said.

3
00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:11.865
"What else can we do?"

4
00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:16.531
"You didn't talk to all the animals," Beatrice said.

5
00:00:16.532 --> 00:00:20.004
"Wild animals are everywhere, you know.

6
00:00:20.005 --> 00:00:22.959
Even in neighborhoods like this."

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.782
"Good point." Daisy told Kaleem what Beatrice had said.

8
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:33.086
"Maybe a bird or squirrel saw what happened to those missing toys," she added.

9
00:00:33.087 --> 00:00:37.175
"Maybe a bird or squirrel stole them," Kaleem said.

10
00:00:37.176 --> 00:00:42.251
"My mom says crows steal plant labels from her garden sometimes."

11
00:00:42.252 --> 00:00:46.162
"Raccoons steal food out of the trash," Daisy said.

12
00:00:46.163 --> 00:00:48.971
Just then she spotted a blue jay.

13
00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:52.817
She asked him if he'd seen the missing toys.

14
00:00:52.818 --> 00:00:56.728
"Are you accusing me of something?" he demanded.

15
00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:03.783
"No," Daisy said. "Er, unless you're the one who took those toys?"

16
00:01:03.784 --> 00:01:07.879
"Absolutely not!" the jay huffed.

17
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.033
Then he cocked his head.

18
00:01:10.034 --> 00:01:14.380
"Although I heard there was a raccoon wandering around last night.

19
00:01:14.381 --> 00:01:18.025
Everyone knows raccoons are thieves."

20
00:01:18.026 --> 00:01:21.992
Daisy told Kaleem what the jay had said.

21
00:01:21.993 --> 00:01:24.928
"Let's go into the forest," Kaleem said.

22
00:01:24.929 --> 00:01:32.798
"We might find a raccoon there."

23
00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:37.664
In the forest Daisy talked to a few animals.

24
00:01:37.665 --> 00:01:46.289
But none of them had seen any raccoons lately.

25
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.950
Finally she asked a chipmunk.

26
00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:53.689
"There's a raccoon sleeping in this tree right now," the chipmunk said.

27
00:01:53.690 --> 00:02:01.143
"Thanks." As the chipmunk skittered off, Daisy called to the raccoon.

28
00:02:01.144 --> 00:02:06.170
A masked face peeked out of a hole in the tree trunk.

29
00:02:06.171 --> 00:02:10.913
"Who are you?" the raccoon asked sleepily.

30
00:02:10.914 --> 00:02:13.146
"Why are you waking me up?"

31
00:02:13.147 --> 00:02:17.067
Daisy explained about the missing toys.

32
00:02:17.068 --> 00:02:21.352
"I don't want to accuse you of anything," she said politely.

33
00:02:21.353 --> 00:02:27.658
"But I've heard that raccoons sometimes, um, borrow stuff."

34
00:02:27.659 --> 00:02:33.984
"I won't deny it," the raccoon said with a yawn.

35
00:02:33.985 --> 00:02:37.001
"But I have no interest in toys.

36
00:02:37.002 --> 00:02:44.177
And while I wouldn't say no to a nice bone, I haven't taken any lately."

37
00:02:44.178 --> 00:02:48.618
"Human girl," a voice said. "I know where you should look."

38
00:02:48.619 --> 00:02:51.351
Daisy turned.

39
00:02:51.352 --> 00:02:55.158
A doe was peering out of some underbrush.

40
00:02:55.159 --> 00:03:07.076
"Follow this trail to the sunny clearing," the deer said before bounding away.

41
00:03:07.077 --> 00:03:14.386
When Daisy and Kaleem reached the clearing, two foxes were sitting on a rock.

42
00:03:14.387 --> 00:03:18.119
They were watching their young cubs play with . . .

43
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.273
"Pet toys!" Daisy cried.

44
00:03:21.274 --> 00:03:25.304
"Hide, children!" the mother barked.

45
00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:29.507
"You don't have to hide," Daisy called.

46
00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.986
"We won't hurt you."

47
00:03:31.987 --> 00:03:36.519
"You can understand what we say?" the father asked.

48
00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:43.829
"Yes," Daisy said. "And now I understand why you took those pet toys.

49
00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.158
But they belong to other animals.

50
00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:49.133
And those animals miss their toys."

51
00:03:49.134 --> 00:03:54.027
"Our cubs need to play," the mother said.

52
00:03:54.028 --> 00:03:59.979
Daisy touched her pocket, which held the money from Finn's owner.

53
00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:05.559
"I know! I'll go to the pet store right now and buy your cubs some toys.

54
00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:09.699
After that, can I return these toys?"

55
00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:16.489
The foxes agreed, and Daisy explained everything to Kaleem.

56
00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:21.279
"Finn and the others will be so happy," he said.

57
00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.579
"The cubs will be happy too." Daisy smiled.

58
00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.349
"You know what, Kaleem?

59
00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:34.906
It feels great to help all kinds of animals!"

